WEBVTT

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.170
It's a fighter plane.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.330
Just one, but would you have us shoot it down?

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.170
Let's do it!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.380
Hold on just a moment...

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.130
It would seem they plan to surrender.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.790
Well that's boring.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.250
But fine, sure.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.040
Took you long enough.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.210
Not by choice.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:24.210
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.710
Kumo to kumo amime o nukete

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:32.250
Odoru hane kaze o matou

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.710
Me no mae de hoshi ga ochiteiku

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.000
Akogareta aoi ao

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.080
Nijimu chihyou keriageta

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.250
Kikasete yo kimi dake no sora no ne o

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.600
Tobidatsu jyuuryoku o mikata ni tsukete

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:09.000
Mou ichido nando demo warai nagara

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:16.040
Bokura wa ushiro o muite tobou to wa shinai

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:21.320
Tsukinai yume asu o otte ikiru

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.750
Waita zetsubou ni ai o tozashita

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.080
Yowai boku wa kirai da

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.040
Nagareru ima mukau saki wa mirai

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.010
The Aggressive Bombers

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.170
A hole...

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.390
...is opening again?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.500
Well we can't exactly say for sure.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.790
But it'll probably open pretty soon.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:49.170
It was all like swirly and fuzzy and stuff.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.330
Kylie, you saw it, too?

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.400
Huh? Yeah.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.040
Why'd you get to? That's not fair!

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.710
The way I see it, a hole didn't open
just once seventy years ago.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.710
But instead lots of different sized ones
have opened up all over a bunch of times.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:07.210
The one seventy years ago just happened
to connect us with the Yufang.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.500
A bunch of times... and just by chance?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.250
Well, color me amazed.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.290
What are you old farts doing here, anyway?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.580
Just paying back a favor.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.050
You did save our hometown, after all.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.140
This is just a hypothesis, but I'd wager a hole is to blame for the

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.930
sea disappearing from Ijitsu, too.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.290
These holes are nothing but trouble!

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.380
Now we can only see the sea in "See the Sea"!

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.540
Councilor Julia. What brings you here?

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.040
Oh, don't you give me that.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.580
You know exactly what's going on!

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.540
I know what, now?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.460
That I'm no "Councilor" anymore!

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.710
Have you resigned?

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:45.130
Those stupid old men and their brainless young
counterparts teamed up to throw me out!

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.460
Accusing me of bribery, embezzlement, even treason!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.920
A cornucopia of crimes!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.170
That's so cool!

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.670
You're far more evil than I imagined!

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.330
What's it gonna be? The death sentence?!

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.880
They're simply trying to frame me!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:55.960
Fabricating offenses is a crime.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.920
Not to that lot, it isn't.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.130
Has Gadoll sided with Isao, then?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.000
There were eight votes to side with him,
one against, and one withheld vote.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.960
So now they're all part of Isao's little club.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.460
You should hear those morons go on about
how we need to dismantle our vested interests.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.500
As if all those interests aren't just getting
gobbled up by Isao himself.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.250
That union he proposes, though...

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.210
The Brotherhood of Freedom Union, was it?

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.790
It doesn't seem like such a bad idea to me.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.500
It's quite logical.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.500
Where's the downside?

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.580
We step up punishments for air pirates,

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:26.700
and the View Security Guard takes care of dealing with 'em all.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.910
All that awaits us in this "world peace" of his is
a complete and total dictatorship under him.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.880
You and that wild imagination of yours!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.630
He doesn't really seem like that bad a guy.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.630
He's good at magic tricks, too!

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.720
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.720
He's the sort of person who works for other's sake.
I have no doubt about that.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.920
Out in the countryside, the union monopoly
has stabilized the prices of goods.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.210
And you don't see poor quality goods making
the rounds anymore either thanks to them.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.420
You don't even notice the choke collar
they've wrapped around your neck, do you?

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:02.130
He'll run the world any way he so pleases.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.710
I don't trust that man, myself.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.670
He seems the sort that lacks the capacity for empathy.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.880
Rahama hasn't really decided on
the whole union issue one way or another yet.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.790
But I figure we'll still manage to get by somehow.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.630
I doubt he'll just let Rahama be.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.540
What? He won't?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.630
What's that you're doing there, Allen?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.830
Just waiting on that curtain call.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:22.630
Like in a play?

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.540
Exactly.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.250
But we won't know if it's a comedy
or a tragedy until after it starts.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.250
Yes, please hold.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.960
Allen...

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:30.510
Allen! It's here!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.000
It's really happening!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:32.890
It's wide open!

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.170
Is it now...

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.850
So I was right about the timing,
but miscalculated the location.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.960
That's really another hole, then?

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.880
That's not really how I imagined them.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:44.460
Is this what you meant when you
said Isao wouldn't let Rahama be?

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:49.330
In hindsight, it seems like he's been after nothing,
but securing these holes for himself the whole time.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.210
That's why he's been ruthlessly hunting down anyone
who tries to learn more about them.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.330
Madame! Madame Loulou!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.330
What's the situation?

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.960
Incoming craft says Shouto's been bombed!
Should we let them aboard?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.170
Give them landing permission.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.880
I'm from the Shouto Vigil-

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.710
I'm Camilla, head of the Shouto Vigilantes.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.540
Has Shouto truly been bombed?

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.080
Why on earth would I lie about that?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.040
Bombed by who, then?

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.710
Planes from Ikesuka!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:30.670
But Shouto has long been an ally to Isao.
Why would they do such a thing?

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.880
Don't ask me!

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:37.120
They just came in all,
"You're plotting against us, aren't you!"

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:42.380
But I knew there had to be some mistake,
so I surrendered right away, being all, "Sorry!"

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.960
But they were just like, "It's too late!"

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.550
Can you believe it?

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.260
This is exactly why we should have
just joined the Union to begin with!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.880
We're gonna be next in their sights!

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.380
Then we need to fight back.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.130
It's not as easy as that.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:56.880
Yeah, we'd be in a world of trouble!

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.270
We could all get killed! Plus...

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.250
We don't really know why it was they bombed Shouto...

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.670
It's because they were no longer any use to Isao!

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.670
Use how?

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.000
Excuse me everyone, but would
you mind taking a look at this?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.790
If you want to know why Shouto was bombed...

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.130
It's because it was the most likely location
for the hole to open over.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.540
But as it turns out, the hole opened up over Rahama.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.130
Are you saying Isao was after this hole?

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.790
Hang on though, aren't you the one
who predicted it would appear there?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.080
How did Isao even know?

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.670
Because he stole all my research from my hospital room.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.010
This here is what I recompiled from what I had left.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.470
He's going to come for that hole no matter what it takes.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.210
You mean he's gonna come bomb Rahama next, then?!

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.580
Excuse me, if I may.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:44.330
I come as a messenger from
the Brotherhood of Freedom Union.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.040
They're one step ahead of us!

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.280
This is a final warning from Chairman Isao himself.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.460
You are to immediately turn over
the fugitive former Councilor Julia.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:58.500
Furthermore, he demands that Rahama
join the Brotherhood of Freedom Union.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:04.880
Fail to meet these terms, and we will be forced
to bomb Rahama in twenty-four hours time.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.090
Truly, truly! A most unfortunate situation.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:13.080
Don't pretend you don't plan on leveling this place
to the ground like you did to Shouta either way!

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:13.880
You brute!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.670
You monster! You demon!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.050
What ever do you mean, Miss Turncoat?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:21.630
Chairman Isao is a most honorable man and issued
his warning a full twenty-four hours in advance.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.730
Not a single life was lost.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.040
That's it!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.290
He just wants the city emptied!

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.210
So he can have the hole all to himself.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.670
His demands are simple.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:38.830
I hope you will speak for all of Rahama now,
and not be tempted by the words of this criminal here.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:39.670
What'll it be?

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.080
I just can't!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.750
What?

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.460
What I'm trying to say is that, well, Rahama is...

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.130
not going to submit to your demands!

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.210
Get lost!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.130
Get lost!

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.080
Get lost!

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.000
Get lost!

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:03.080
Get lost!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.600
Well, that is most unfortunate.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.960
Get lost!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.290
Perhaps today was just not a good day?

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.040
Get lost!

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.170
Get lost!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.420
Not that you'll have any better days now.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.080
Get lost!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.130
Get lost!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:14.210
Nice work!

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.040
Mayor!

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:15.830
You sure showed 'em!

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:16.790
Nicely done!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.030
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:02.290
What a boorish man he is to think he can just burn
down a town and send its people fleeing on a whim!

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:06.910
If he wishes to stomp out all resistance,
it is both an appropriate and logical strategy.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.880
Magic-man has really let me down! Hmph!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:14.580
Let me guess, you're wondering if it was those
around him who are really pulling the strings.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.220
Something's just off about
burning down whole cities like this...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.630
We've never flown this high before!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.590
That doesn't mean you can't!

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.550
I want to knock out their numbers
before they make it to Rahama.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:02.380
The only problem is our firepower and ability to reload.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.390
That's where my secret weapons come in!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:10.420
We've got their route locked down. Plenty of eyewitness
reports, and we got 'em right on our radar, too.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.130
The perfect situation for an ambush.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.540
Just the time for my Raiden to take the spotlight!

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:19.000
What the?!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.170
It's freezing up here.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.250
But it's so quiet, too.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.790
And the sky's so blue.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:37.000
I wish Ol' Sab was here to see this.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.050
I wonder if he's already seen it, though.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.040
This is it!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.040
Got a hit! But that thing's still flying!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.580
Fall back! Everyone head for the Hagoromo!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.420
This isn't it for us, after all!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.920
I wanna shoot some more rockets!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.510
I sure wish I was shooting down fighters instead.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.260
Enemy formation incoming!

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.140
We've got three large aircraft about fifty kilo-khrill! away!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.640
Keep us updated.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.830
I feel like it's getting even bigger.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:16.460
It's holding its form, too.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.210
I wonder how big it is now.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.080
I want priority put on ammunition!
Don't worry about fuel, just fill up what you can.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.630
Anyone who slacks gets a thirty-seven milimeter
shoved right up their rear!

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:33.580
Roger!
By all means!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.910
Hurry up!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.000
Looks like our friends here got
tighter turning than we do!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.760
Don't go flying into friendly crossfire!

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.720
We've got three enemy bombers!
Closing in at twenty-five kilo-khrill!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.580
My, my... Are we going to make it?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:04.540
Shoot!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.670
Kept you waiting, huh?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.130
Take that!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.870
Chika's here!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.540
Enemy bombers only 13 kilo-khrill away!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.540
Don't let them drop those bombs on Rahama!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.750
All vigilantes focus on those escort fighters!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.880
Leave the bombers to the KOTOBUKI Corps!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.350
Jeez, these things are enormous!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.180
All the easier to land hits on, don't you think?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.230
What are these things made of?!

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:49.210
Dangit! They're not going to make this easy, are they?

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:52.580
I think that makes us even!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.460
You really saved me there!

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.830
Not yet we haven't! Look!

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.170
Only 3 kilo-khrill until they reach Rahama!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.630
Aim for the base of their main wings!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.460
Follow my lead!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.790
Hey, hey! Why don't we just blow up
those bombs of theirs?

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.050
That's unrealistic.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.040
Is it?

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.930
Those bombs are well armored.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.140
And piercing that plating won't be enough to set them off!

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:23.330
We did it!

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.710
Finally got one down. Only two to go!

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:30.460
They're just two kilo-khrill out!

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:32.710
We don't have enough time...

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:33.500
Don't give up!

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.000
What the heck?!

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.210
If they're shooting with us, I don't care who they are!

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:58.040
Who knows why they're here,
but we've got one target left!

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:58.830
We can do this!

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.600
Grrr, agh! Fine!

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:10.580
We're too late!

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:13.130
Dangit!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.240
It's gone...

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.330
The hole seems to have disappeared.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:55.750
What?! It did?! Why?!

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.750
Unfortunately I cannot answer that.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.950
Aww shucks, it's gone then?

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:03.670
I guess I should have been out there flying myself.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.540
I'll be taking my plane out next time.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.960
Preparations are already complete.

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:12.460
They took down all but one of those bombers.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:17.380
That may be enough to sway
other cities quaking in fear over them.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:18.640
That's giving it a positive spin.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.110
Why you...!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:42.750
Kylie! What do you think you're doing?!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.250
She's in her "Thunderbolt" mode now.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.500
What's that even supposed to mean?

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.330
She's like an angry thunder cloud, now.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.250
There's no stopping her until she's vented all her rage.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.960
She only has three minutes of fuel remaining.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.590
I'm going to shower.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.830
Gotcha!

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:39.510
You stinkin'-

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.290
What's your deal?!

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:46.330
Why do you always have to be
such a pain and get in my way?!

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:47.460
You really piss me off!

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:49.880
You're a girl?! Who are you?

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.540
I'd like to ask you the same thing!

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:56.080
How many times have I driven you away just
to have you come chasing after me again all pushy?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.670
Come on then, spit it out! Who are you?
Or what, you don't got a name?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.170
I do have a name! I'm Kylie, okay?!

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.920
Oh, don't you give me that! Cut it with the attitude!

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:05.790
I don't care who you are or
what rock you crawled out from underneath!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.620
I'm Naomi.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:07.540
Naomi...?

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.830
I figured you'd be some big dumb oaf of a guy,
but you're just and old hag, huh?

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:14.580
If I'm a hag, then you're just
some snot-nosed little wanton bitch of a girl.

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:15.290
Wha...

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.250
And a shitty pilot!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.050
Oh yeah?!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.290
Shoot me down then, if I'm wrong!

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:24.600
You're lucky I'm so kind that I'm talking with you here,
but I don't know or care who the heck you are!

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.420
And I don't know or care who you are either!

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:31.100
But why the heck are you out here helping us now
when you were just some air pirate before?!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.580
Well why should I have to be stuck
in the same place forever, huh?

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:38.360
I don't care for your stinking teams or alliances.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.960
I hate all that crap. I do what I want, when I want!

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.750
What's wrong with that? Nothing, that's what!

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.790
I bet you thought I was your enemy this whole time.
You did, didn't you?

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:50.830
Well sucks to be you! I'm not your friend or your foe.
It just depends on what mood I'm in.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:51.580
You're full of it!

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.130
Full of what? Why?

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:57.880
I sided with Julia-what's-her-face this time, but that's
just cause she makes more sense than Isao-whatever.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.880
Now can you quit trying to slap
your stinkin' labels on me?

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:04.080
You sure are ignorant for such a young kid!
Ugh, I can't stand it!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.760
Don't you agree?

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.170
Oh, I definitely do.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:07.850
Yeowch!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.500
And you know what I can't stand
the most about you? That mark of yours!

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.130
My mark...?

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:13.380
Don't play dumb with me!

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.980
That mark on your tail there was
my stinkin' mentor's mark.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.920
Now, I don't know where you caught a peek
of that mark there, but let me set you straight.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.790
Quit copying it you stinkin' little boy!
Or girl, or whatever!

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:27.460
Ol' Sab taught you?!

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.040
You know Ol' Sab? How?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.830
Are you his wife?!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.920
The hell I am! What are you,
his daughter or something? Granddaughter?!

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:33.420
No!

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:34.330
Then what, then?

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.540
I don't even know...

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:45.960
Huh, so that crabby old man was
always like that then, eh?

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:46.680
Yup!

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.710
So, Miss Naomi was it? Were you his student?

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.040
Just Naomi's fine.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.750
It was about eight years ago, now.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.960
After you met him, I guess.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:00.920
We met kinda the same way you and I just did,
and a lot happened from there.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:02.170
A lot...?

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:05.460
Yup, and I ended up learning under him.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:10.580
I learned from him, stole his techniques,
and promised myself I'd shoot him down someday.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:13.660
Ooh! I kinda wanna hear what
went down between you two.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:19.790
But that lecherous perv of an old fart just took off
one day without so much as a word to anyone!

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.800
He never changes, does he?

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.170
Aww, did he abandon you? You poor thing.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.170
He abandoned you, too!

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.670
I guess we're a pair of abandoned sisters, then.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:30.830
Imagine that!

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:34.640
Eww, that's horrible for one,
and also just gross and wrong!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:38.670
I'm gonna find that geezer some day
and send him off to hell.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.920
Then we'll be even.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.750
What do you fly for, Naomi?

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:47.630
Feels good, right? Being up there.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:49.630
Do you need more reason than that?

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.170
I love anything that feels good!

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:08.630
Ano sora o jiyuu ni kakenukete mitai to

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:12.430
Hanasaki no kaze ni negai o noseta

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:16.380
Akogare ga keshiki o tsukutteiku

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:20.790
Ano toki no kaze wa genki kanaa

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:29.130
Nan no tame ni tatakau no kana

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:33.170
Koko ni iru riyuu wa nan darou?

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:41.420
Toikaketa sora wa kotaenai kedo

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:49.080
Bokura wa tsubasa o motteiru

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Haruka kanata nageki no shuuchakuten

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.040
Mitsuketa monogataritachi

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:05.790
Kono sora wa dare ni mo ubaenai

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:10.500
Boku wa kakeru nanimo kowakunai yo

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.670
Shiawase nara koko ni aru yo

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.510
Preview

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:37.960
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"Duel in Ikesuka"!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:41.040
Duel in Ikesuka
